Jahshaka patch 0050 — the irradiance field's const-buffer size (which the pin
under-reported by one float4) and the zero auto-multiplier in VctLighting.

SOURCE patch. EVERY TREE MUST RE-RUN `irisgl/scripts/build-ogre.sh` after
pulling this (reset the ogre-next submodule first if it already carries an
earlier revision of any patch: `git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next checkout -- .
&& git -C irisgl/thirdparty/ogre-next clean -fd`). It OVERLAPS patch 0044
(OgreIrradianceField.cpp) and patch 0037 (OgreVctLighting.cpp): it applies on
top of them, in stack order, and a per-patch reverse-check on a tree that
carries 0037/0044 reports this one "unapplied" for those files — judge by
content (CLAUDE.md, the overlap blind spot).

AMENDED 2026-09-17 (lane FIELD-RASTER-CRUD). Two of the four original items
existed only for the irradiance field's RASTERISED probe source, which was
deleted that day together with patch 0023 (its media half): the public
`switchToRasterSource()` plus the four read-only accessors it came with
(audit F3), and patch 0023's C++ half, the `invFieldSize` push in
`IrradianceFieldRaster::renderProbes` (audit F4). Both hunk sets are gone from
this file; nothing in Jahshaka calls `IrradianceFieldRaster` any more, so the
pin's own copy of that class is left exactly as upstream ships it. What remains
is what the VOXEL-fed field and VctLighting need:

  1. `IrradianceField::getConstBufferSize()` UNDER-REPORTS BY ONE float4 (F2).
     It returned `sizeof(float) * (4*3 + 4 + 4)` = 80 bytes, while
     `fillConstBufferData` writes an `IrradianceFieldRenderParams` of 96 — a
     float4x3, then numProbesAggregated + 2 pads, then the depth pair, then the
     IRRADIANCE pair — and the struct the generated shader declares
     (`Hlms/Pbs/Any/IrradianceField_piece_ps.any`) is those same 24 floats. So
     HlmsPbs reserved 16 bytes too few for the pass buffer and advanced its
     write pointer by 20 floats after a 24-float write. Upstream's own samples
     simply overrun their pass-buffer map by 16 bytes; with an HlmsListener next
     in line (ours), the listener's first float4 lands on top of
     irradBorderedRes / irradFullWidth / irradInvFullResolution and every
     irradiance UV collapses onto texel 0 — DDGI contributes an almost-black
     constant, with no error anywhere. Engine-side, this was a
     reserve-four-floats-and-skip-them in `FogHlmsListener` that only worked
     because HlmsPbs happens to fill the field's block BEFORE calling the
     listener; it was deleted with this patch.

  2. `IrradianceFieldGenParams::unused0` WAS UPLOADED UNINITIALISED on every
     voxel-sourced update (the raster branch memsets the struct; the voxel
     branch writes every member except this one). Zeroed where the rest of the
     struct is written.

  3. `VctLighting::update`'s AUTO MULTIPLIER TURNS "NO LIGHTS" INTO "NO GI"
     (F10). The maximum radiance over the scene's visible lights is 0 in a scene
     with none; the code inverted it unconditionally (+inf), so
     `mInvBakingMultiplier` came out 0 and the shader's
     `blendWeight = blendFade * blend * multiplier` was 0 for every voxel. A
     bound VctLighting also switches the PBS ambient pieces off inside its
     volume, so an ambient-lit scene whose only lamp is switched off went BLACK
     the moment VCT was enabled. The zero case is folded into the branch that
     already exists for "no measurement wanted" (`autoMultiplier == false` →
     `mBakingMultiplier`), which is the same answer the engine was choosing from
     outside — by walking EVERY node in the scene before every injection
     (`OgreScene::hasVctLights`, three call sites) to decide whether to pass
     `autoMultiplier = false`. That walk is deleted with this patch; the three
     call sites pass `true`.

VERIFICATION. `git apply --check` against the pristine pin with the stack up to
0049 applied, and `git apply --reverse --check` after applying; `build-ogre.sh`
re-run in the lane worktree; `--engine-selftest` byte-identical — all three
items are no-change-by-construction on the shipped default scene (1: the
listener skipped the same four floats it now no longer has to reserve; 3: the
engine already passed the value this branch now computes), which the lanes
measured rather than assumed. The GI suites (gi.ddgi_*, gi.modes, gi.tiers,
gi.budget, gi.coalesce) are the behavioural gate.

